from pathlib import Path
import json,numpy as np
import matplotlib
matplotlib.use('Agg')
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
O=Path(__file__).parent;fit=json.loads((O/'bank-history-delay-fit.json').read_text());hist=np.load(O/'bank-history-asymmetric_threshold-0.npz');fig,axes=plt.subplots(3,3,figsize=(14,10))
for col,(day,start) in enumerate([('2026-01-03',447),('2026-02-15',402),('2026-02-15',3387)]):
 a=np.load(O/(day+'-physical-input.npz'));i=np.searchsorted(a['t'],start);tt=np.arange(76)*.04;j=fit['validation_windows'].index([day,start]);lat=np.load(O/f'{day}-{start}-effective-lateral.npz');rf=np.load(O/f'{day}-{start}-rate-first-shared.npz')
 axes[0,col].plot(tt,a['brake_mm'][i:i+76,0],label='Left');axes[0,col].plot(tt,a['brake_mm'][i:i+76,1],label='Right');axes[0,col].set_title(('Hood River' if day.endswith('03') else 'Trout Lake')+f' | {start} s')
 axes[1,col].plot(tt,np.rad2deg(hist['truth'][j]),color='black',lw=2,label='Flight');axes[1,col].plot(tt,np.rad2deg(hist['model'][j]),label='Bank + actuator history');axes[1,col].plot(tt,np.rad2deg(lat['model'][:,0]),label='Coupled lateral');axes[1,col].plot(tt,np.rad2deg(rf['model'][:,0]),label='Rate-first',ls='--')
 axes[2,col].plot(tt,np.rad2deg(lat['truth'][:,1]),color='black',lw=2,label='Flight');axes[2,col].plot(tt,np.rad2deg(lat['model'][:,2]),label='Coupled lateral');axes[2,col].plot(tt,np.rad2deg(rf['model'][:,2]),label='Rate-first',ls='--')
 for ax in axes[:,col]:ax.grid(alpha=.2);ax.set_xlabel('Forecast time (s)')
for ax,label in zip(axes[:,0],['Nominal line pull (mm)','Payload bank (deg)','Heading change (deg)']):ax.set_ylabel(label);ax.legend(fontsize=8)
fig.suptitle('Causal replay: recorded brake input and competing response models',fontsize=16);fig.tight_layout(rect=(0,0,1,.95));fig.savefig(O/'iteration-causal-lateral.png',dpi=150);plt.close(fig)
p=O/'physics-development.html';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8');section='''<section id="causal-lateral-audit"><h2>Replay-input audit and causal lateral comparisons</h2><p>Raw ATT, RCOU, IMU and XKF1 timestamps are strictly increasing in both main logs. Reconstructing the brake travel directly from RCOU reproduces both replay arrays exactly. Hood River contains a 69-second raw logging gap; it must remain excluded through the airborne/valid-data masks. This audit does not establish actuator latency, only clock ordering and mapping consistency.</p><figure><img src="iteration-causal-lateral.png" alt="Recorded left and right brake commands with bank and heading predictions from causal diagnostic models"><figcaption>Each forecast starts from the recorded attitude and a body-rate estimate using only the last three gyro samples. The bank model also initializes its input filter from four seconds of preceding commands. All three displayed model structures still miss important maneuvers; none is an accepted flight simulator. Airspeed is held at its inferred initial value within each three-second diagnostic.</figcaption></figure><p>A pure-delay sweep from 0 to 0.4 seconds trades against the fitted response time but does not resolve the flight-to-flight mismatch. An explicit bank/heading/course model likewise fails to generalize. Expanding training to 316 windows, balanced across flight and manual/assisted groups, does not fix its high-bank predictions. Five additional Trout Lake blocks centered on 1150, 1750, 2250, 2850 and 3170 seconds are quarantined from that training for later testing.</p><p>A reduced brake-to-turn-rate model, with bank following lateral acceleration, also fails in shared and separately calibrated flight cases. This rules out that tested first-order structure; it does not imply that brake-induced yaw is absent physically. Causal initialization and actuator history are retained in the validation workflow. Evidence: <code>replay-input-audit.json</code>, <code>bank-history-delay-fit.json</code>, <code>effective-lateral-fit.json</code>, <code>broad-lateral-fit.json</code>, and <code>rate-first-fit.json</code>.</p><h2>SolidWorks API access established</h2><p>A read-only typed API query returned the saved assembly's mass properties: mass 0.87164 kg, assembly-coordinate center [0.03461, −0.00179, 0.07847] m and principal inertias [0.002318, 0.003280, 0.003851] kg m². These describe the CAD model, not the complete flying configuration. Component coverage, density assignments, axis mapping and missing hardware must be reconciled before using them as flight inertia. The current component reader preserves the open CAD session and does not save the model.</p></section>'''
if 'id="causal-lateral-audit"' not in s:p.write_text(s.replace('</html>',section+'</html>'),encoding='utf-8')
